what_to_check_after_slicing:
Physical test, against the current reference piece, under raking light and with the silk highlight moved across the surface:
  - upper outer slopes and bird body, Z 32-52;
  - inside of the ring, lower half (hole floor, Z 8-24);
  - head tops, Z 56-64.

  Look for a diagonal or wavy gyroid pattern with about 3 mm pitch, dull or striped bands, or ridges at layer steps. Also check the head tops for pillowing or pinholes. Press lightly on the slopes to compare stiffness with the reference.
